WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:07.480
Hey, be careful! You might think you're
never going to fall, but we all know

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.480
someone who has, don't we?
Next time, it could be you.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.600
The good news is most
falls are preventable.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:20.240
Start with six easy steps. First, find
a balance or exercise program to help

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.000
you build stability,
strength, and flexibility.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.580
Make it fun, and go with a friend.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.240
Don't be afraid to tell your doctor
if you've had a fall or are afraid of

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.320
falling. Ask her to assess
your risk of falling.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.240
Discuss medications with
your pharmacist or doctor.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.340
They'll know what prescriptions and
over-the-counter medications can increase

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.600
your risk of falling. Make sure you
get your vision and hearing checked every

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:52.500
year because your eyes and ears are
key to keeping you on your feet.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:58.460
Keep your home safe. For example,
remove any items you might trip over.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.780
Make sure your home is well lit.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.500
Use bath mats in your shower and
install grab bars in the bathroom.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.860
And finally, remember, it's
important to talk to your family.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.060
Ask for their support in taking
these simple steps to stay safe.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.120
Falls are not a normal part of aging,
but every 13 seconds, an older adult

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:25.440
visits an emergency room
for a fall-related injury.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.480
Luckily, you can take
steps to reduce your risk.
